Well, in NetHack, the wand of undead turning in its effects is sometimes a
word-joke.

When you use it on, say, an ape corpse, the corpse isn't turned undead,
but un-dead instead. Ie, it's turned alive.

Actually, the game seems to remember what a corpse was before it became a
corpse. For example, you can have a human corpse that turns into a vampire
when "turned undead", while another human corpse would turn into a human
zombie, dependant on what it was before you killed it.

